<title>USA: Settlement in General Motors GM  suit - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Settlement in General Motors GM  suit - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A settlement agreement was approved by a Louisiana judge in a long-disputed C/K pickup truck class action case but with a provision that could prompt an appeal from General Motors Corp  GM.N.</p>
<p>The settlement calls for GM to give $1,000 coupons to more than five million pickup owners, the story says.</p>
<p>But the settlement also will require GM to pay about $28 million in fees and expenses to plaintiffs attorneys and &quot;former objectors,&quot; the story says.</p>
<p>GM says it is considering appealing the $28 million tab, the story says.</p>
</text>
